# Never publish these — the repo is public.
#
# supabase/ is the three Edge Functions. They are deployed straight to
# Supabase with `supabase functions deploy` -- Vercel never serves them
# and the public site never needs them. Publishing them hands over the
# list of RPCs, the shape of every authorization check, and the
# assistant's system prompt. Same argument as the schema below: not a
# key, but a map. They live in the private repo.
#
# package.json / package-lock.json exist only to pin build-clean.js's
# four dependencies (terser, acorn, node-html-parser, typescript). The
# site itself has none and loads nothing from npm at runtime; a
# package.json in the public repo would suggest otherwise and invite a
# `npm install` that has nothing to do with deploying.
#
# VERCEL.md is deployment documentation, and goes with README.md.
#
# The tooling (sync-*.js, check-drift.js, build-clean.js) is private
# for the same reason. None of it is served, none of it is a secret,
# and all of it describes the site's internals in detail -- sync-csp.js
# alone spells out the whole content-security policy and where each
# directive comes from. Work in the private repo; publish the subset.
#
# deploy-schema.sql is the whole database design. Not a key (security
# lives in the database, not in secrecy) but a free map for anyone
# poking at the API. Deleting a file later removes it from the site but
# NOT from git history — add it here before the first `git add`.
deploy-schema.sql
supabase/
sync-csp.js
sync-vendor.js
sync-sri.js
check-drift.js
build-clean.js
email-*.html
README.md
VERCEL.md
LEGAL-COMPLIANCE.md
DEPLOY.txt
package.json
package-lock.json
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
node_modules/

# ---- current build note (2026-08-09) ----
#
# Half self-hosted. supabase-js is served from vendor/supabase.js on
# every page and cdn.jsdelivr.net is gone from script-src entirely.
# xlsx is still loaded from cdn.sheetjs.com by soa.html alone, because
# 0.20.3 exists nowhere else -- npm's newest xlsx is 0.18.5 and carries
# CVE-2023-30533.
#
# So vendor/ and vendor-lock.json DO exist here and the section below
# applies. `node sync-vendor.js` fetches the remaining file and closes
# out the last CDN origin; build-clean.js refuses to build if anything
# under vendor/ that a page references is missing.

# ---- what is deliberately NOT ignored ----
#
# vendor/ and vendor-lock.json are TRACKED, on purpose.
#
# vendor/ holds supabase-js and xlsx, served from this origin so
# script-src can stay 'self' alone. Ignoring them would mean the
# deployed site is missing the two files every page depends on, and the
# symptom is a portal that renders and then does nothing at all.
#
# vendor-lock.json is the record of which bytes were vetted. Committing
# the libraries without it leaves nothing to check them against, which
# is most of the point — see sync-vendor.js.

# ---- Edge Functions: now in this repo ----
#
# Three Supabase Edge Functions are invoked by name from the client.
# They used to have no source here, which meant a deploy from this repo
# alone produced a portal where approval emails silently failed,
# deleting a user threw, and the assistant was dead -- three separate
# faults that did not look related and none of which pointed here.
#
# Recovered from the live project 2026-08-09 and committed under
# supabase/functions/<slug>/index.ts:
#
#   notify-approval    approval.js  -- approval/rejection emails
#   admin-delete-user  approval.js  -- wraps admin_delete_user_data()
#                                     plus the Auth Admin API, neither
#                                     of which belongs in the browser
#   ai-assistant       page-dashboard.js -- the chat panel
#
# All three read their keys from Deno.env. No secret is in the source
# and none may be added: they are set with `supabase secrets set` and
# live only in the function runtime. The patterns below keep the local
# files those secrets land in from ever being committed.
supabase/.env
supabase/.env.*
supabase/.temp/
.env
.env.*

# ai-assistant does NOT call ai_assistant_take_token(), despite that
# function existing, being granted to authenticated, and being the
# only thing ai_assistant_usage is for. The rate limit is not in
# force. See the Edge Functions section of README.md.
